      "message": "wait, \n1) data_ptr points inside the common buffer, into which we read the file in get_file_or_die(). and in get_file_or_die() we allocate exactly the file length. so, if the file size is not 4-bytes aligned we risk reading past the end of this buffer when transferring the last section.\n2) we actually transmit garbage for unaligned-sized data: start of the next section or random data after the end of the last section.\n\nto deal with (1) we can malloc(len+3) in get_file_or_die(). not sure how critical (2) is, but to deal with it we may want to track data_len and actual_data_in_buf_len and for the last tpm_send_pkt()/transfer_block() first copy into an intermediate buffer, set the extra bytes to zero, and then sending from there.",
